Description: TPM2-sealed TOTP codes shown before disk unlock
 tpm2-kira seals a TOTP secret into TPM NVRAM under a PCR policy and prints the
 current code from the initramfs, before the root filesystem passphrase is
 requested. A code that appears proves the measured boot chain still matches the
 state the secret was sealed against; a missing code means something in that
 chain changed.
 .
 Recovery runs through a PolicyOR branch authorised by an ECDSA signing key, so
 a legitimate firmware or bootloader update can be re-bound with
 "tpm2-kira reseal" without re-enrolling the authenticator app.
 .
 On Debian the codes are shown from an initramfs-tools init-premount script, so
 no systemd in the initramfs is required.
